@startuml readme-topology
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the README's how-it-works diagram (readme-topology.svg) and how the README's hero.gif is made
' covers: README.md
' covers: _spec/_assets/hero.gif
' covers: _spec/_assets/readme-topology.svg
'
' ── RENDER (DECIDED 2026-11-17) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' GitHub renders no PlantUML, so the README embeds this file's SVG:
'   mise x conda:plantuml@1.2026.10 -- plantuml -tsvg _spec/_assets/readme-topology.puml
' NOT CHOSEN: Mermaid (a second diagram language beside every spec); ASCII
' boxes (static, and unlike the spec look).
' The shape follows the run form's topology strip
' (_spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml): host → sbx microVM → sbx proxy → cloud.
'
' ── THE HERO GIF (MEASURED 2026-11-17) ──────────────────────────────────────
' hero.gif is `proveo run claudecode` on a git copy of e2e/samples named acme:
' the scope page, page 2, then devices → browser ticked; it loops there.
' Tools, all through mise, none in [tools]: tmux 3.7b (mise.toml), uv 0.13.8
' (Python with pillow + fonttools), ffmpeg 9.0.2 (conda), gifsicle 1.98 (conda).
'   1. a detached tmux, 110×32, runs bash with PS1='$ ' and env TERM=xterm-256color
'      COLORTERM=truecolor PROVEO_WIZARD=on PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE=0, a fresh
'      PROVEO_HOME and PROVEO_STATE_ROOT, USER=LOGNAME=you (the strip's host
'      label) and OLLAMA_HOST at a closed port; send-keys types and navigates.
'   2. every 50 ms: `tmux capture-pane -e -p` plus #{cursor_x} #{cursor_y}
'      #{cursor_flag}; only changed frames are kept, with their timestamps.
'   3. a renderer draws each frame at Menlo 15 px on #1e1e2e (box drawing
'      drawn as lines; fallbacks Apple Symbols, Arial Unicode, STIX Two Math
'      for ⚿); a tab moves to the next 8-column stop.
'   4. ffmpeg concat (per-frame durations) → demo.mp4 (libx264 yuv444p crf 10)
'      → fps=12 palettegen/paletteuse (128 colours, no dither) → gifsicle -O3
'      --lossy=20. 107 frames, 1026×674, 22 s, 215 KiB.
' Two edits, both host noise: the GIF ends before Esc (the exit line prints a
' log path under the recording machine's home), and the ~1 s hand-off frame
' between the pages is dropped, since it showed this host's "sbx 0.54.0 is not a
' version proveo has verified" note. A verified sbx prints no such note.
' The recorder was a throwaway script; this note is the way to redo it.
' HISTORY: until 2026-11-17 the GIF came from a vhs tape (hero.tape), deleted.

left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 60

actor "you" as You
node "host · macOS · Linux" as Host <<host>> {
  component "**proveo**\nrun form · sbx Kit · .env" as CLI <<app>>
  database "~~/.proveo\nsessions · toolchains" as Home <<db>>
  component "Ollama · Chrome\nopt-in host services" as HostSvc <<app>>
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM <<host>> {
  component "**agent**\nclaudecode · codex · cursor\nopencode · hermes" as Agent <<app>>
  database "repo clone\nbrowser · android add-ons" as Clone <<db>>
}
component "**sbx proxy**\nholds your API keys" as Proxy <<async>>
cloud "LLM providers\nallowed domains" as Cloud <<cloud>>
database "your repo\nrefs/proveo/<sid>" as Repo <<db>>

You ARROW_MAIN CLI : proveo run <agent>
CLI ARROW_MAIN VM : sbx create · run
CLI ARROW_QUEUE Home : sessions persist
Agent ARROW_MAIN Clone : edits · commits
Agent ARROW_CLOUD Proxy : egress under sbx policy
Proxy ARROW_CLOUD Cloud : key attached
Agent ARROW_OPTIONAL HostSvc : host.docker.internal
Clone ARROW_MAIN Repo : teardown · proveo adopt
@enduml
